# What Vercel uploads.
#
# The repository is large — the Rust target directory alone is gigabytes, and
# the Flutter SDK and the local dev stack are not part of the deployment. Vercel
# uploads everything not ignored, so this file is not an optimisation: it is
# what keeps the upload to a size the platform accepts.

# Build artifacts. The Rust build happens on Vercel's builder, and the
# Flutter build happens in the build command.
target/
**/target/
**/build/
**/.dart_tool/
**/.gradle/
**/node_modules/
**/.git/

# The local cross-compilation directory for the Vercel function. It is a
# Linux build of the same source the builder compiles, kept for local
# experiments; it is 380 MB and has no business in the upload.
.vercel-target/

# The Flutter SDK, when `scripts/build-vercel.sh` has installed it locally
# instead of on the builder.
.flutter-sdk/

# The Flutter Web bundles are built by `scripts/build-vercel.sh` during the
# build, so the checked-in copies are not uploaded. `public/` is the output
# directory: it IS uploaded, and the build command rewrites it in place.
apps/shop_web/build/
apps/admin_web/build/
apps/line_web/build/
apps/shop_app/build/

# Local development state.
.vercel/
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.local
shots-local/
**/shots-local/
logs/
**/logs/
nul

# The k3s deployment manifests and the container build context. They describe
# a different deployment (a cluster behind Envoy) and the merged edge
# supersedes them for this one.
#
# `services/deploy/` is NOT excluded: the function version lives there, and
# the functions' entry points under `api/` include their implementation from
# `services/deploy/vercel/src/`. Excluding it would leave the build without
# the code it compiles. The cluster version's own directory is excluded by
# the `k3s/` pattern below.
k3s-deploy/
docker/
k3s/

# The game-server images. They build the RGS player-service and admin-service
# containers for the k3s/Envoy deployment, which this deployment replaces.
# They are also a hazard here: a Dockerfile anywhere in the uploaded tree
# makes Vercel detect the container preset, and the container preset serves
# the game server and ignores both the function and the static build. The
# images are built from git by .github/workflows/docker-build.yml and
# gm-backend-publish-ghcr.yml, so excluding them from the upload costs the
# pipeline nothing.
Dockerfile
Dockerfile.*
**/Dockerfile
**/Dockerfile.*

# Documentation and design notes. They are not part of the deployment.
docs/
docs-parallel/
graphify-out/
.audit-reports/
.autopilot/
.audit/

# Editor and OS noise.
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
